## SUMMARY: How Agents Fit Into Kynetic Spec

### Design Pattern:

```
┌─ DEFINITION LAYER (Schema)
│  └─ Agent = {id, name, capabilities, dispatch rules, skills, adapter, budget, concurrency}
│
├─ RUNTIME LAYER (Dispatch Engine)
│  └─ Watch task state changes → Match against agent.dispatch rules → Queue invocations
│
├─ INVOCATION LAYER (Ralph / Manual)
│  └─ Spawn agent via adapter (ACP protocol) → Run with skills → Record session
│
├─ AUTOMATION LAYER (Ralph Loop)
│  └─ Orchestrate autonomous iterations: work → review → reflect
│
└─ DELIVERY LAYER (Setup)
   └─ Detect environment → Install hooks → Render skills → Generate instructions
```

### Key Files & Line Counts:
- **Schema** (`src/schema/meta.ts`): Agent structure definition
- **Dispatch** (`src/agent-runtime/dispatch.ts`): State-change matching
- **Ralph Command** (`src/cli/commands/ralph.ts`): Loop orchestration
- **Ralph Framework** (`src/ralph/*.ts`): Supporting modules (2,237 lines)
- **Setup** (`src/cli/commands/setup.ts`): Environment configuration (1,600+ lines)
- **Tests** (`tests/ralph*.test.ts`, `tests/agent*.test.ts`): 4,416+ lines

### Absolute File Paths (for reference):
- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/schema/meta.ts`
- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/agent-runtime/dispatch.ts`
- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/cli/commands/ralph.ts`
- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/cli/commands/agent.ts`
- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/cli/commands/setup.ts`
- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/src/cli/commands/agents.ts`
- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/kynetic.meta.yaml`
- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/kspec-agents.md`
- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/templates/agents-sections/06-ralph-loop.md`
- `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/templates/skills/manifest.yaml`

This comprehensive system enables **self-hosting automation**: agents are defined in meta, matched by the dispatch engine, spawned via adapters, and guided by skills—all while using kspec itself to manage the work.